cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its reported results, please cite this repository and record the commit used."
type: software
title: "Adaptive tree-neurons: function-preserving growth and controlled capacity allocation"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-18"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/adaptive-tree-neurons"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/adaptive-tree-neurons"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Research software for allocating affine specialists to selected individual
  neurons through function-preserving centered-gate insertion. The implementation
  includes compact PyTorch layers, first-step scoring and exact parent-conditioned
  joint ridge scoring with greedy selection, matched random and ordinary-capacity
  controls,
  complete-state checkpoint recovery, native tabular baseline adapters and
  source-bound paired experiments. Planted controls demonstrate learnable
  added capacity. In the completed sixteen-problem development study with two
  paired repeats per problem, ordinary continuation beat joint growth on every
  problem average and had 15.6 percent lower mean exploratory evaluation error.
  Joint growth had 1.25 percent higher mean error than matched random placement.
  The tested selector branch closed negative. Native validation surveys are
  exploratory; the full tuned benchmark and protected evaluation were unfinished
  at project sunset on 21 October 2026.
  No practical superiority, independent confirmation or model-family novelty is
  claimed. Public source, reports and selected audit evidence remain; project-local
  raw archives were removed at sunset, limiting full raw-result authentication.
keywords:
  - neural network growth
  - affine stumps
  - capacity allocation
  - gated linear units
  - reproducible research
  - negative results
